9. NO-DOCKER-LOADER PROBE (failure mode)
================================================================================
$ env PATH=/usr/bin:/bin railpack build "$ROOT/vite-spa" \
    --name localhost/easy-host-vite-spike:nodocker --progress plain
... all steps CACHED ...
#21 exporting to docker image format
#21 exporting layers done
#21 exporting manifest sha256:af0c99bfcceb47ce5d41a44c0b6f2040966363f85d674a7ccdfa3367479b5586 done
#21 exporting config sha256:28b0d46c8389652847b345a47d2bbb92fb6aada6380b2de020698a3f0591ddf2 done
#21 sending tarball
<no output for 300 s; command killed by timeout>

Interpretation: Railpack 0.43.0 shells out to `docker load` after a successful solve.
When the binary is absent, the loader goroutine dies and nothing drains the image
pipe, so the build hangs forever at "sending tarball" instead of failing.
The same build completes in 1.42 s when /usr/local/bin/docker (the podman shim) is present.

